{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.NegativePeel","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTransfer"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.markov_cox_eq_quantumTrace'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.markov_cox_eq_quantumTrace'","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L329-L339","doc":"**The torus-braid value of every Markov trace with `z_D`, at `n + 1` sites.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.quantumTrace_cox_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.quantumTrace_cox_level","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L314-L327","doc":"The normalised quantum trace of a torus braid does not depend on the number of spectator\nsites: it may be computed at `n + 1` sites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.extend_cox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.extend_cox","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L305-L312","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.markov_cox_eq_quantumTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.markov_cox_eq_quantumTrace","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L288-L301","doc":"**Transfer to the quantum trace.** Any normalised, cyclic Markov trace with `z = z_D` on any\nalgebra carrying a Hecke family `(N, q − q⁻¹, 1)` takes, on every torus braid\n`(s₀ ⋯ s_{n−1})^p` with `n ≤ N`, the value of the normalised quantum trace on `V^{⊗(N+1)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_cox_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_cox_pow","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L276-L286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_markov","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L269-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_cyc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_cyc","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L263-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace_one","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L260-L261","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.presTrace","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L255-L258","doc":"**Ocneanu's trace on the presented algebra**, for every `N`: the model trace pulled back\nalong `lift`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_markov","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L245-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.val_mem_adjoin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.val_mem_adjoin","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L234-L243","doc":"Elements of the generated subalgebra of the model are generated by the matrices `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_cyc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_cyc","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L218-L232","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_one","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L214-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau_apply","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L210-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.tau","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L199-L208","doc":"**The normalised quantum trace** on the model algebra,\n`τ(x) = (1 + q²)^{−(N+1)} · tr(W · x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.trace_W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.trace_W","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L191-L197","doc":"The trace of the site weight is `(∑ w)^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA_heckeFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA_heckeFamily","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L186-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA_val","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L184-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sA","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L181-L182","doc":"The Hecke family inside the model algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S_mem","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L175-L179","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.A","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L172-L173","doc":"The model algebra at level `N`: the centraliser of `W` in `End(V^{⊗(N+1)})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.trace_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.trace_markov","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L140-L168","doc":"**Markov property of the quantum trace at every level.** For `k < N` and `X` in the\nsubalgebra generated by `S₀, …, S_{k−1}` on `V^{⊗(N+1)}`,\n`tr(W · (X · S_k)) = z_D · tr(W · X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.adjoin_succ_eq_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.adjoin_succ_eq_map","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L128-L136","doc":"The subalgebra generated by the first `k ≤ N` generators one level up is the image of the\none at level `N` under the site extension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.extend_S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.extend_S","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L123-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.strand_heckeFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.strand_heckeFamily","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L98-L119","doc":"**The strand braidings form a Hecke family** with `a = q − q⁻¹`, `b = 1`, for every `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sum_wt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.sum_wt","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L86-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.S","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L81-L84","doc":"The strand braiding `σ_i` on `V^{⊗(N+1)}`, ℕ-indexed (`0` from `N` on). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.zD","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L78-L79","doc":"Convention D's Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.W","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L74-L76","doc":"The site weight `W` on `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.wt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorMarkovModel.wt","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TensorMarkovModel.lean#L71-L72","doc":"The weight `w = (1, q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}